[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4755330785","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120465#issuecomment-4755330785","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120465","id":4755330785,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG3CW4Q","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T22:56:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T22:56:14Z","body":"I suggest [compiling a Godot build that includes debug symbols](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/engine_details/development/compiling/compiling_for_windows.html) (`debug_symbols=yes` SCons option), and running it from a command prompt until it crashes. This way, you can get an usable crash backtrace you can paste here.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4755330785/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4756037904","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120465#issuecomment-4756037904","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120465","id":4756037904,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG3thEA","user":{"login":"Pixelmusement","id":78319361,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MzE5MzYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78319361?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement","html_url":"https://github.com/Pixelmusement","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pixelmusement/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T02:17:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T02:17:39Z","body":"While I would be willing to utilize a debug-enabled build of 4.7 in my workflow until the next crash to get that backtrace, I don't have ANY of the things required to compile the Godot Editor/Engine and the only one I even know how to use from past experience is MSVC, but I haven't even touched a modern copy of MSVC since 2012. Is there another way to get a debug-enabled build of Godot without building it myself?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4756037904/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4863920715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120465#issuecomment-4863920715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120465","id":4863920715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIemKSw","user":{"login":"saierXP","id":45038185,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDM4MTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45038185?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP","html_url":"https://github.com/saierXP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T08:50:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T08:50:50Z","body":"> Is there another way to get a debug-enabled build of Godot without building it myself?\n\n@Pixelmusement You can download the artifacts zip I built with Actions, or you can fork [my actions repository](https://github.com/saierXP/Godot-Custom-Build-Templates) to enable the free GitHub Actions function.\n\nhttps://github.com/saierXP/Godot-Custom-Build-Templates/actions/runs/28568715878\nCreate a `run.bat` command file in the same path and replace `project_path` with your project path. After running, a `log.txt` file will be generated to record the crash message.\n```bat\n@echo off\nrem Force search for debugging symbols in pdb under the same path.\nset _NT_SYMBOL_PATH=%~dp0;SRV*C:\\Symbols*https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols\n\nrem replace to your project folder path\nset project_path=\"\"\n\n\"%~dp0godot.windows.editor.dev.x86_64.exe\" -e --path \"%project_path%\"  2> \"%~dp0log.txt\"\n\npause >nul\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4863920715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4872673869","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120465#issuecomment-4872673869","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120465","id":4872673869,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIm8aTQ","user":{"login":"ds84182","id":2268005,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjgwMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2268005?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182","html_url":"https://github.com/ds84182","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ds84182/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T04:46:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T04:46:21Z","body":"Since you're on Windows there should be crash information in Event Viewer. At the very least it should reveal the module (DLL or EXE) that caused the crash. It should be event 1000 or 1001 in application logs.\n https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/windows-server/performance/troubleshoot-application-service-crashing-behavior\n\nIt is entirely possible that it's a crash in the GPU driver, rather than Godot.\n\nUnless you have tons of applications logging or constantly crashing you should be able to find a recent crash.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4872673869/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4979375777","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120465#issuecomment-4979375777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120465","id":4979375777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKMs-oQ","user":{"login":"mikerofone","id":588648,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4ODY0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/588648?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone","html_url":"https://github.com/mikerofone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikerofone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T10:07:57Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T10:07:57Z","body":"Hi,\n\nI'm using Godot 4.6.3 stable on Linux Mint (Cinnamon, Xorg) and have had three hangs of the editor in the last 10h of usage just after a tooltip opened as well. I don't recall that happening when I was last using Godot 9 months ago, which was at version 4.5 but also with older drivers etc.\n\nWhat's different for me from what the OP described:\n\n1. The editor doesn't auto-close, it just hangs indefinitely and requires me to kill the hanging process.\n2. The tooltip **does** show, and in fact it will overlap other applications' windows when alt-tabbing.\n\nThe editor doesn't seem to be stuck in an endless loop, as it has very low CPU usage while hanging (certainly not pinning an entire core).\n\nI all instances I had my game running at the time of the hang. Killing the game's process first didn't un-hang the editor.\n\nMy tech info from the help menu:\n```\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Linux Mint 22.3 (Zena) on X11 -\nX11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) -\ndedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 Ti (nvidia; 580.159.03) - \nAMD Ryzen 5 2600 Six-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.53 GiB memory\n```\n\nDon't have much other debug info to add at this point, but wanted to provide an additional data point.\n\nCheers\nmikerofone","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4979375777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]